      "id": "fast-downsample",
      "name": "FastDownsample",
      "category": "ImageBuilder",
      "signature": "FastDownsample(Target, Sub Steps, Zero Value, Average Func)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "TImageBuilder*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Sub Steps",
          "type": "Int"
        },
        {
          "name": "Zero Value",
          "type": "PixelType&"
        },
        {
          "name": "Average Func",
          "type": "TFunctionRef<PixelType ( PixelType,int )>"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "TImageBuilder<PixelType>",
      "docs": "Very basic downsampling technqiue that just averages NxN pixel blocks. Multi-threaded.\n@param SubSteps each NxN pixel block of this size is averaged into 1 pixel in the output image\n@param Zero value to use with template PixelType must be provided, pixel values will be added to this value\n@param AverageFunc Called with Sum(Pixels) and PixelCount, return value is used as new pixel value (eg should be average)"
    },
    {
      "id": "f-image-adapter",
      "name": "FImageAdapter",
      "category": "ImageBuilder",
      "signature": "FImageAdapter(Target, Image)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Target",
          "type": "TImageBuilder*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Image",
          "type": "TImageBuilder<float>*"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "Void",
      "docs": "FImageAdapter is a wrapper around different types of TImageBuilder that provides a\nstandard interface, which allows functions that don't need to know about the specific\nimage type to operate on \"any\" image. For example to allow code that works on a 4-channel\nimage to operate on a single-channel image (in which case the Adapter will expand/collapse\nthe channels automatically)."
